    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Gastonia's AC Repair Specialists</p>
      <h2>Why Gastonia Homeowners <em>Choose Us</em></h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Gastonia summers push residential cooling systems to their limit. When your AC
        struggles in 95°F heat, you don't have time for guesswork — you need a
        <strong>licensed local specialist</strong> who knows Gaston County homes,
        responds the same day, and repairs it right the first time.
      </p>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3>Same-Day Diagnosis & Repair</h3>
          <p>Most <strong>Same-Day AC Repair</strong> calls in Gastonia are completed within hours of your call — no multi-day waits, no rescheduling loops.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">🏅</div>
          <h3>Licensed & Certified</h3>
          <p>Every technician is licensed, certified, and trained on modern refrigerants — including <strong>Refrigerant Leak Repair</strong> and system recharges.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">💵</div>
          <h3>Upfront Pricing, Zero Surprises</h3>
          <p>We quote before we wrench. No hidden fees, no upsell pressure — just honest <strong>Central AC Repair</strong> and service at fair Gastonia market rates.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">📍</div>
          <h3>Local to Gaston County</h3>
          <p>Based in Gastonia — we know the neighborhood, the housing stock, and the AC brands most common in local homes. Faster response, better context.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="serving">
        <strong>Proudly Serving Gastonia & All of Gaston County</strong><br />
        Belmont · Bessemer City · Cramerton · Dallas · Lowell · Stanley · and surrounding communities
      </p>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">47 min</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Avg. Response</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">98%</span>
          <span class="stat-label">First-Visit Fix Rate</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">24/7</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Emergency Service</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problems -->
  <section id="problems" class="section problems">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Common AC Problems in Gastonia Homes</p>
      <h2>Recognize <em>These Signs?</em></h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Gastonia's heat and humidity accelerate AC wear. If your system shows any
        of these symptoms, don't wait — small issues compound fast in summer conditions.
      </p>
      <div class="problems-grid">
        <article class="problem-card urgent">
          <h3>Frozen Coils</h3>
          <p>Ice on your indoor or outdoor unit means restricted airflow or a <strong>refrigerant leak</strong>. Running a frozen AC causes compressor damage — needs <strong>Emergency AC Repair</strong>.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-danger">Urgent — Act Now</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card urgent">
          <h3>Blowing Warm Air</h3>
          <p>If your AC runs but blows warm, refrigerant is likely low or your <strong>compressor</strong> is failing. In Gastonia summers, this is a true emergency — same-day service recommended.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-danger">Urgent — Act Now</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card urgent">
          <h3>Leaking Water</h3>
          <p>Water pooling around your unit signals a blocked condensate drain or frozen coil melting. Unchecked, this causes mold growth and ceiling damage — call today.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-danger">Urgent — Act Now</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card">
          <h3>Weak Airflow</h3>
          <p>Low airflow from vents usually signals a clogged filter, failing blower motor, or collapsed ductwork. Often a quick fix — but left alone it overloads your <strong>compressor</strong>.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-warn">Address Soon</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card">
          <h3>Thermostat Issues</h3>
          <p>A system that short-cycles, won't turn on, or ignores temperature settings often has a faulty <strong>Thermostat</strong> — an inexpensive fix that restores full comfort quickly.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-warn">Address Soon</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card">
          <h3>Strange Noises</h3>
          <p>Banging, squealing, or grinding sounds point to loose hardware, worn bearings, or a failing <strong>compressor</strong>. Unusual AC sounds almost always mean a component needs attention.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-warn">Address Soon</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card">
          <h3>Inconsistent Cooling</h3>
          <p>Hot rooms, cold rooms, and uneven comfort across floors usually indicate duct leaks, refrigerant imbalance, or an undersized system struggling through Gastonia heat.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-info">Monitor Closely</span>
        </article>
        <article class="problem-card">
          <h3>Rising Energy Bills</h3>
          <p>A sudden spike in your Duke Energy bill while keeping the same temperature is your AC working harder than it should — dirty coils, low refrigerant, or a failing motor are common culprits.</p>
          <span class="badge badge-info">Monitor Closely</span>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-box">
        <p>Seeing Any of These Signs? Don't wait for a full breakdown in the Gastonia summer heat.</p>
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get a Quote — {phoneDisplay}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services -->
  <section id="services" class="section services">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Residential Air Conditioning Repair — Gastonia, NC</p>
      <h2>Expert AC <em>Repair Services</em></h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Every cooling problem has a root cause. Our certified technicians are trained
        to <strong>diagnose accurately and repair correctly</strong> — whether it's a
        worn compressor, refrigerant loss, or a simple thermostat fault.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <article class="service-card highlight">
          <span class="service-tag">Urgent Response</span>
          <h3>Emergency AC Repair</h3>
          <p>When your cooling system fails at the worst possible moment, every minute of Gastonia heat matters. Our <strong>Emergency AC Repair</strong> service is available around the clock — no after-hours surcharges.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Available 24 hours, 7 days a week</li>
            <li>Average on-site response under 60 minutes</li>
            <li>Fully stocked service vehicles — most repairs same visit</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Request Emergency Service</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Most Common</span>
          <h3>Central AC Repair</h3>
          <p>Central cooling systems are the backbone of Gastonia home comfort. Full-system <strong>Central AC Repair</strong> — from condenser and evaporator coil service to blower motor replacement and refrigerant recharge.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>All major brands — Carrier, Trane, Lennox & more</li>
            <li>Full system diagnostics included</li>
            <li>Written repair estimate before any work</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Get a Quote</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Ductless Systems</span>
          <h3>Mini-Split Repair</h3>
          <p>Ductless mini-splits demand specialized knowledge. Trained in <strong>Mini-Split Repair</strong> for all major brands — diagnosing communication faults, refrigerant issues, and board failures.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Learn More</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Critical Component</span>
          <h3>Compressor Repair</h3>
          <p>The compressor is the heart of your AC system. <strong>Compressor Repair</strong> requires precision — we accurately diagnose whether repair or replacement is the right call.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Learn More</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Certified</span>
          <h3>Refrigerant Leak Repair</h3>
          <p>Low refrigerant means warm air and rising energy bills. Certified technicians perform <strong>Refrigerant Leak Repair</strong> — locating the source, sealing it, and recharging to spec.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Learn More</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Quick Turnaround</span>
          <h3>Thermostat Repair</h3>
          <p>A faulty control interface causes short-cycling and wasted energy. <strong>Thermostat Repair</strong> or upgrade is one of the fastest ways to restore comfort and lower your bill.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Learn More</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Fast Service</span>
          <h3>Same-Day AC Repair</h3>
          <p>No multi-day waits. <strong>Same-Day AC Repair</strong> means you call in the morning and sleep in comfort that night. Available throughout Gastonia and Gaston County.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Book Today</a>
        </article>
        <article class="service-card">
          <span class="service-tag">Preventive Care</span>
          <h3>Drain Line Cleaning</h3>
          <p>Blocked condensate drains are a leading cause of AC water damage. <strong>Drain Line Cleaning</strong> prevents overflow, mold, and costly repairs — recommended every cooling season.</p>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Learn More</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Urgency CTA -->
  <section class="section urgency">
    <div class="container urgency-inner">
      <div>
        <span class="urgency-badge">● Priority Service Available Now</span>
        <h2>AC Down in the Gastonia Heat?</h2>
        <p>Don't suffer through a North Carolina summer without cooling. If your system stopped working, is blowing warm air, or is making unusual sounds — our <strong>Emergency AC Repair</strong> team can respond today.</p>
      </div>
